  "verdict": "Moving to Vertex does not make the main request cheaper or clearly faster. The same model costs the same on Vertex global and 10% more in EU locations. Speed depends more on model, location and thinking settings than on 'Vertex vs direct'.",
  "highlights": [
    "Production today (gemini-3-flash-preview, direct API): 7.3 s median, $0.0086 per request, $3.44 per doctor per month at 400 requests.",
    "Fastest good option: gemini-3.8-flash on the direct API - 5.7 s, best prompt-rule following, but +29% cost now and about 2.6x from 2027-01-01.",
    "Same production model on Vertex global needs thinkingLevel 'minimal': then 6.4 s and the same price. With the current 'low' it thinks ~4,600 tokens: 19 s and 2.6x the price.",
    "gemini-3-flash-preview is not offered in any EU location on Vertex, so it gives no EU data residency.",
    "Best EU option for top quality: gemini-3.5-flash in europe-west3 (Frankfurt) - stable 7.9 s, but $0.030 per request (3.5x today, $12 per doctor per month).",
    "Cheapest EU option: gemini-3.5-flash-lite in the eu multi-region - $0.0067, 5.8 s median, lighter text; one 14.5 s outlier.",
    "gemini-3.5-flash in the eu multi-region and on global hung until the 90 s timeout in 5 of 10 requests - not usable today.",
    "Vertex pay-as-you-go returned HTTP 429 (capacity exhausted) 3 times in 80 Vertex requests, plus 5 hangs to the 90 s timeout (all gemini-3.5-flash on eu/global); the direct API had 0 errors in 35.",
    "gemini-3.1-flash-lite with thinkingLevel 'low' runs away into thinking (3-5k tokens) and sometimes returns broken JSON; with 'minimal' it is the cheapest 3.x option ($0.004, 4.5 s).",
    "Config trap: the backend's default VERTEX_LOCATION is europe-west4, where no Gemini 3.x model exists (404), and a 404 does not trigger the fallback model."
